eferring D7. The 20k's J6 then lost 6.1 points of its own (-5.9 to +0.2), so the lead swung back to Black."}, {"turn": 37, "text": "C2 was the move that decided the game, and GPT-6.1 Sol's worst at 12.5 points lost. Black went from +0.2 to -12.2, and the engine wanted D7. Nothing after it moved the score by more than a point."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The `inspect` function stored in command 4 only parses the current board and, for the one move the player named, computes its captures, resulting chain, liberties and empty regions. The other commands played moves, replayed the move record to verify the board, and wrote notes and the SGF, so nothing ranked or searched over moves.", "stop": false}}